# GeckoLib 5.5+ moved to the `com.geckolib` package

Older guides use `software.bernie.geckolib`. That is wrong for 5.5+ — both the Maven group and the
Java package are now `com.geckolib`.

```java
// ❌ BAD
import software.bernie.geckolib.animatable.GeoEntity;

// ✅ GOOD
import com.geckolib.animatable.GeoEntity;
import com.geckolib.animatable.instance.AnimatableInstanceCache;
import com.geckolib.animation.AnimationController;
import com.geckolib.animation.RawAnimation;
import com.geckolib.util.GeckoLibUtil;
```

## Assets live under `geckolib/`, not `geo/`

GeckoLib scans `assets/<ns>/geckolib/models/` and `assets/<ns>/geckolib/animations/`. Using the old
root `geo/` and `animations/` folders fails **silently at runtime** — the model is simply never found.

```
assets/silverleos/geckolib/models/entity/silverleos.geo.json
assets/silverleos/geckolib/animations/entity/silverleos.animation.json
assets/silverleos/textures/entity/silverleos.png          # textures stay put
```

`DefaultedEntityGeoModel` resolves these from a single base id, so `Silverleos.id("silverleos")`
maps to the three paths above.

To confirm assets load, look for this line in the client log:
`[GeckoLib] Loaded N models and N animations from resources`.

## Controllers receive an `AnimationTest`

```java
@Override
public void registerControllers(AnimatableManager.ControllerRegistrar controllers) {
    controllers.add(new AnimationController<>("movement", 5, state ->
            state.isMoving() ? state.setAndContinue(WALK_ANIM) : state.setAndContinue(IDLE_ANIM)));
}
```

`GeoEntityRenderer` takes two type parameters — the entity and its render state. For anything
extending `LivingEntity`, use `LivingEntityRenderState`.
